  "title": "Timer-started Pre-Vote round survives leader establishment and makes the new leader re-elect",
  "cause": "handle_tick_election starts a Pre-Vote round for a Candidate whose election timed out; establish_leader/become_leader do not clear pre_candidate, and handle_pre_vote_resp calls elect() on the round's quorum without re-checking role or vote.",
  "trigger": "With enable_pre_vote, a candidate's real election outlives its election timeout (e.g. slow vote persistence); the timer starts a Pre-Vote round at term+1; the real quorum then makes it Leader; the round's quorum arrives afterwards.",
  "consequence": "The established leader starts a new election at term+1 without any external request or higher term: leadership is abandoned and the term inflates; the stale Leader object (vote behind state.vote) trips the try_leader_handler assertion (RaftCore panic in debug builds) and, in release builds, the cluster stayed leaderless with the term inflating.",
  "sites": [
    "openraft/src/engine/engine_impl.rs:establish_leader",
    "openraft/src/engine/engine_impl.rs:handle_pre_vote_resp",
    "openraft/src/core/raft_core.rs:handle_tick_election",
    "openraft/src/engine/handler/vote_handler/mod.rs:update_internal_server_state"
  ],
  "actions": [
    "TickPreElect",
    "HandleVoteResponse",
    "HandlePreVoteResponse"
  ],
  "invariants": [
    "TickPreVoteRoundNotHeldByLeader",
    "LeaderNotPreemptedByTimerPreVote"
  ],
  "premises": [
    "Pre-Vote is enabled (Config::enable_pre_vote or runtime toggle) and the cluster has more than one voter.",
    "A candidate's real election can complete after its election timer fired but before the vote RPC timeout (election_timeout_min).",
    "Only do_elect and become_following clear pre_candidate.",
    "The PreVoteResponse runtime gate checks only pre_candidate presence and leader-id equality."
  ],
